=================================

In Mac commmand space then type terminal when opens type below command to install mysql
  brew install mysql
  
  
  Step : Start the MySQL Service
Once the installation finishes, you need to kickstart the server engine in the background:


Bash
brew services start mysql

Step : Log In
Wait about 5 seconds for the database to initialize, then run the login command:

Bash
mysql -u root

(Note: If you have not set a password yet, omit the -p. If you already set a password previously, use mysql -u root -p instead).

===============================

mysql> show databases;
+--------------------+
| Database           |
+--------------------+
samplestruts

CREATE TABLE bankuser (name VARCHAR(20), password VARCHAR(3), address VARCHAR(35));


mysql> INSERT INTO bankuser (name,password,address) VALUES ('bankuser','pwd','nyc');
Query OK, 1 row affected (0.14 sec)

mysql>

===================================================================================
Enter Exit to exit from mysql on mac terminal

To install DB UI tool like DBeaver give brew command like below

brew install --cask dbeaver-community


Step : Launch DBeaver in Mac
Press Command + Space to open Spotlight Search.

Type DBeaver and press Enter.

(Alternatively, open your Finder, click on Applications in the sidebar, and double-click DBeaver).

Step : Connect DBeaver to Your Local MySQL
When DBeaver opens for the first time, it might automatically prompt you to select a database. If it doesn't, click the Plug Icon with a Plus Sign (New Database Connection) in the top-left corner.

Select MySQL from the list of database types and click Next.

Set up the connection fields using your current settings:

Host: localhost

Port: 3306

Database: samplestruts

Username: root

Password: (Leave this completely blank)

